1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,960
I could write any
word, except that one.

2
00:00:03,170 --> 00:00:04,530
Help was always to me.

3
00:00:04,530 --> 00:00:06,320
And I always came alone.

4
00:00:06,520 --> 00:00:09,100
So I bent my last
tube into one letter.

5
00:00:09,700 --> 00:00:12,100
And through the wall,
my mother bent hers.

6
00:00:12,690 --> 00:00:13,560
Us.

7
00:00:14,460 --> 00:00:16,170
And the whole street answered.

8
00:00:17,470 --> 00:00:19,830
Stop that! You'll
break the ring!

9
00:00:19,830 --> 00:00:21,950
Sir, I'm going to have
to ask you to leave.

10
00:00:22,150 --> 00:00:25,350
Fool! Break the ring,
and they all go out!

11
00:00:25,450 --> 00:00:27,450
Out. Yes. That's the idea.

12
00:00:28,650 --> 00:00:29,890
And out they came.

13
00:00:29,890 --> 00:00:30,240
Ruth.

14
00:00:30,240 --> 00:00:30,590
Otis.

15
00:00:30,590 --> 00:00:33,240
Pete, still asking
about his oven.

16
00:00:33,630 --> 00:00:35,140
The other me took my hand.

17
00:00:35,140 --> 00:00:37,020
And then there was just me.

18
00:00:38,220 --> 00:00:39,550
Mara?

19
00:00:39,850 --> 00:00:40,820
Mom.

20
00:00:41,430 --> 00:00:43,220
Look how tall you are.

21
00:00:43,310 --> 00:00:44,750
You left your coat.

22
00:00:45,450 --> 00:00:47,590
I'm not crying.
I'm leaking argon.

23
00:00:48,100 --> 00:00:51,430
By morning, every light on
the street was just a light.

24
00:00:51,730 --> 00:00:51,980
Mara?

25
00:00:51,980 --> 00:00:53,850
When did we get a number eleven?

26
00:00:54,250 --> 00:00:55,750
And somebody knocked.
